Imports:
  - Types:
      - RecipientId
    From: app/src/main/java/org/thoughtcrime/securesms/recipients

Annotations: |
  This cell is the app's persistence layer boundary. SignalDatabase is a single SQLCipher
  database aggregating dozens of table objects behind one companion-object facade (only one,
  `RecipientTable`, is documented here as representative of the convention — the same
  constructor-injection-of-(context, databaseHelper) and `DatabaseTable` base shape applies to
  every other table in this directory). Every table extends `DatabaseTable`, which is how writes
  reach `DatabaseObserver` to notify the UI layer of changes, rather than each table implementing
  its own notification plumbing.

---

"SignalDatabase(context: Application, databaseSecret: DatabaseSecret, attachmentSecret: AttachmentSecret)":
  location: SignalDatabase.kt
  annotations: |
    The single SQLCipher-backed database instance for the app, and the aggregation point for
    every table object. Application code almost never touches an instance directly — it goes
    through this type's own companion-object accessors instead (see recipients, messages,
    below).

    `context`: application context.
    `databaseSecret`, `attachmentSecret`: encryption key material for the database file and for
    attachment bodies stored outside it.
  properties:
    "isPrimaryDatabase -> Boolean": |
      True for the app's real, on-disk database; false for the in-memory instances tests
      construct to exercise a single table in isolation.
  methods:
    "init(application: Application, databaseSecret: DatabaseSecret, attachmentSecret: AttachmentSecret)": |
      Creates the process-wide singleton instance if one does not already exist. Called once,
      early in application startup, before any table accessor is used.
    "recipients() -> table:RecipientTable": |
      The single, process-wide `RecipientTable` instance. Companion-object accessors of this
      same shape exist for every other table (messages(), threads(), groups(), etc.).
    "runPostSuccessfulTransaction(dedupeKey: String, task: Runnable)": |
      Schedules `task` to run once, after the current write transaction commits successfully;
      calls sharing the same `dedupeKey` within one transaction collapse to a single execution.
    "runPostBackupRestoreTasks(database: Any)": |
      Runs the app's post-backup-restore maintenance pass: replays schema upgrades against the
      restored file, then clears out tables (job/megaphone/key-value/constraint/dependency
      state) that must never be carried over from a backup as-is.

"DatabaseTable(context: Context, databaseHelper: SignalDatabase)":
  location: DatabaseTable.java
  annotations: |
    Base type every table class in this cell extends. Owns the shared notification plumbing so
    individual table classes never call `DatabaseObserver` directly by name — they call one of
    these protected helper methods instead.

    `context`: application context.
    `databaseHelper`: the owning SignalDatabase instance, providing access to the underlying
    readable/writable SQLite handles.
  methods:
    "getReadableDatabase() -> db:SQLiteDatabase": |
      A handle suitable for read queries.
    "getWritableDatabase() -> db:SQLiteDatabase": |
      A handle suitable for writes.
    "notifyConversationListeners(threadId: Long)": |
      Notifies observers registered for the given conversation thread that its content changed.
      Subclasses call this after a write that affects that thread's messages.

"DatabaseObserver()":
  location: DatabaseObserver.java
  annotations: |
    Central pub/sub hub tables use to notify the UI layer of data changes, so the UI does not
    need to poll and tables do not need their own bespoke listener plumbing.
  methods:
    "registerConversationObserver(threadId: Long, listener: Observer)": |
      Subscribes `listener` to changes affecting the given conversation thread.
    "registerConversationListObserver(listener: Observer)": |
      Subscribes `listener` to changes affecting the top-level conversation list (new/removed
      threads, not per-message content).
    "unregisterObserver(listener: Observer)": |
      Unsubscribes a previously-registered `Observer`, regardless of which register* method it
      was registered through.
    "notifyConversationListeners(threadId: Long)": |
      Notifies observers of thread `threadId` that its content changed.
    "notifyConversationListListeners()": |
      Notifies observers that the top-level conversation list changed.
    "notifyRecipientChanged(recipientId: RecipientId)": |
      Notifies observers that the recipient identified by `recipientId` (from Imports) changed.
    "notifyMessageInsertObservers(threadId: Long, messageId: MessageId)": |
      Notifies observers that a specific new message was inserted into thread `threadId`.

"RecipientTable(context: Context, databaseHelper: SignalDatabase)":
  location: RecipientTable.kt
  annotations: |
    Representative table class — the same (context, databaseHelper) constructor and
    `DatabaseTable` base shape documented here apply to every other table in this directory
    (MessageTable, ThreadTable, GroupTable, and the rest), which are not individually
    documented in this cell.

    `context`, `databaseHelper`: as `DatabaseTable`.
  methods:
    "getByE164(e164: String) -> id:RecipientId": |
      The `RecipientId` (from Imports) for the recipient with the given phone number, if a row
      already exists for it.
    "getByServiceId(serviceId: ServiceId) -> id:RecipientId": |
      The `RecipientId` for the recipient with the given service identifier, if a row already
      exists for it.
    "getAndPossiblyMerge(serviceId: ServiceId, e164: String, changeSelf: Boolean) -> id:RecipientId": |
      Finds the recipient matching `serviceId` and/or `e164`, inserting a new row if neither
      matches an existing one; if both match different existing rows, merges them into one and
      returns the surviving id.

      `changeSelf`: whether the local user's own recipient row is allowed to be the merge target.
    "getRecord(id: RecipientId) -> record:RecipientRecord": |
      The full stored record for `id`. Throws if no row exists for that id.
    "getBlocked() -> blocked:List<RecipientRecord>": |
      Every recipient the local user has blocked.
    "getExistingRecords(ids: Collection<RecipientId>) -> records:Map<RecipientId, RecipientRecord>": |
      Stored records for every id in `ids` that currently exists; ids with no matching row are
      simply absent from the result rather than causing an error.

